Z||000005||bHooper||05-18-2001||12:55 PM||||i forgot to add that i'm flying into Pittsburgh (using some coupons for a free flight).  so a round trip rental wouldn't exactly be economical.<P>anyway, so here's waht i found out on purchasing 3.4's locally...  most places are crazy!  they generally want $7-900 for an engine with 70,000 miles or more on it!<P>i found one low mileage engine (37,000 miles) for $800.  i also found one fella that may just be crazy enough to qualify as a potential Fiero owner!  in fact, when i asked for a 3.4, he said "what you doing, puttingit in a Fiero?" Gafaw!!  when i said "YES!" he proceded to tell me that he stuffs 350's in sunbirds!  he also said that he could get 3.4's for $650 with 30-40,000 miles on them.  he even told me of a place to have the block modified.<P>conclusion?  maybe i should go to this fella and get a 3.4, or see what he is doing to these sunbirds... maybe i can learn something usefull that can be applied to the fiero!<P>oh yeah, i forgot to add that i checked with a local engine exchange place, on swapping the 2.8 for a reman. Grooms 2.8... they wanted $2100!!!  (this after chuckling on the phone with the engine source!)  BmA!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>hoop||||reg||1
